# Architecture Pattern

## Core Structure
- Follow modular layered architecture: DTOs → API → Services → UI → Pages
- Each resource follows identical folder structure pattern

## File Organization
- DTOs: `src/api/dto/[resource-name]/[ResourceName]Dto.ts`
- API: `src/api/integration/[ResourceName]/[ResourceName]Api.ts`
- Services: `src/services/[resource-name]/hooks/use[ResourceName].ts`
- Pages: `src/pages/[category]/[resource-name]/index.tsx`
- Always update corresponding index.ts files for exports

## Naming & Style
- Comments/docs: en-US
- Code identifiers: English (camelCase for variables/methods, PascalCase for types/components)
- Database tables: snake_case (`resource_name`)
- DTOs follow pattern: `[ResourceName]ViewDto`, `[ResourceName]SaveOrUpdateDto`, `[ResourceName]DeleteDto`
- API methods follow pattern: `get[ResourceName]sApi`, `saveOrEdit[ResourceName]Api`, `delete[ResourceName]Api`

## API & Data Handling
- Use Supabase for all database operations
- Always convert between camelCase (frontend) and snake_case (backend)
- Implement pagination, sorting, and filtering consistently
- Use hooks with useCallback for API interaction
- Maintain separation between business logic and UI

## Implementation Consistency
- Reuse existing patterns for all new features
- Follow existing project component patterns
- Use existing utility functions for common operations (keysToCamel, keysToSnake)
- Keep all CRUD operations consistent across resources
